    "description": "# DL-5: Link Object + Assignment Fields\n\n_Establish the Link object and its assignment-control fields, tied to a Deal._\n\n### FIELDS\n\n* Link ID (auto-numbered)\n\n* Link Code\n* Tracking URL (long text)\n* Assignment Cap — renamed from \"Cap\"\n* Active (checkbox) — controls CMS-dropdown availability\n* Internal Notes\n\n### IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS\n\n* \"Cap\" is renamed to \"Assignment Cap\"; 0 means unlimited.\n* Active controls whether the link is available in the CMS assignment dropdown.\n* Link Code stays non-unique for now, matching current team usage. Uniqueness is a future business-process goal, not part of this build.\n\n### NOTES\n\n* Provenance: DL-5 (Deal Record User Stories doc).\n* Open question (not resolved in the transcript): Salesforce URL fields cap at 255 characters and truncate silently — worth confirming Tracking URLs (with UTM params, etc.) will reliably fit before build.\n\n### SOURCE\n\n* [Deal Record User Stories — Google Doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IIfaPIol2HmX8v09gw0SKQyCuoHTiwrJxdDNc7qtvB8/edit)\n* [Aug 18 Weekly Sync — Emily Vandenberg, 43:22 (Assignment Cap rename + CMS dropdown behavior)](https://fathom.video/calls/787411922?timestamp=2602)\n* [Aug 18 Weekly Sync — Kobi Kunasekaran, 42:56 (0 = unlimited)](https://fathom.video/calls/787411922?timestamp=2576)\n* [Aug 18 Weekly Sync — Joyce Kiddell, 40:34 (Link Code non-unique for now)](https://fathom.video/calls/787411922?timestamp=2434)\n* Dependencies: [BUILD-212 — Deal: Object + Core Details](https://app.asana.com/0/0/1217693597664441/f/)\n* Owner (proposed): Taryn Reithofer\n* Created 2026-08-20 from Deal record documentation review.\n\n",
